## Context

Reading-2 findings 8, 22, 23, 24 (tracker 0578). Global sweep over
main.tex, run after the whole main.tex chain so it catches what the
regional rewrites left behind. Line numbers below are pre-chain ground
truth — re-grep everything.

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.tex` — whole file
- `src/aedist/matching/lp.py` — matcher implementation (header says
  "Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) assignment problem")
- `tests/test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py:428` — verbatim-anchor
  test: the KEPT analysis-cohort prompt quote contains Doc-07-era
  sentences; the sweep must not alter quoted prompt text

## Actions

1. (8, 24) Sweep ALL internal codenames out of reader-facing prose:
   Doc-07 (pre-chain sites L510, L511, L710, L1417, L1419, L2193),
   ADR-3 (L1839), and grep for the classes `Doc-\d`, `ADR-\d`,
   `exp[0-9]_`, ticket numbers, and similar repo-internal identifiers.
   Replace with reader-facing descriptions ("the naive prompt", "the
   matching-cost design choice"). Verbatim-quoted prompt text is
   exempt (it is a quoted artifact).
2. (22) Main text (§1–§9 + Conclusion) must not refer to code — file
   paths, function names, module names belong in annexes only. Sweep
   `\fpath{`, `\texttt{` and prose code mentions in the main sections;
   move load-bearing detail to the relevant annex; figure captions
   refer to annexes for details.
3. (23) The matching algorithm has a name — use it consistently
   instead of bare "the LP matcher" repetitions. DISCREPANCY TO
   VERIFY: the author says the name is "flow", but the code calls it
   a MILP assignment / LP matcher and main.tex says "LP matcher"
   (L1019, L1096, L1359, L1832, L1878). Check whether the
   implementation is a min-cost-flow formulation (assignment problems
   are) or whether docs/ name it; if the evidence does not support
   "flow" as the established name, name it per the code and flag the
   divergence in the PR description for the author — do not invent.

